# `@repo/fonts`

Centralizes the same **local font files** and **`next/font/local`** loaders used by the storefront so other Next apps (e.g. `@repo/social`) stay typographically aligned.

## Layout

- **Font binaries:** [`packages/fonts/assets/`](packages/fonts/assets/) (woff2 Peyda, Peyda Fanum, Rokh, Kaghaz — copied from the former `apps/frontend/public/fonts` tree).
- **Loaders:** [`packages/fonts/src/index.ts`](packages/fonts/src/index.ts) exports `peyda`, `peydaFanum`, `rokh`, `kaghaz` (same CSS variables: `--font-peyda`, `--font-peyda-fanum`, `--font-rokh`, `--font-kaghaz`).

## App setup

1. `"@repo/fonts": "workspace:*"` in the app `package.json`.
2. `transpilePackages: [..., "@repo/fonts"]` in `next.config.ts`.
3. **Root layout:** put `${…variable}` classes on `<html>` and apply `${peydaFanum.className}` on `<body>` when the default UI text should match the storefront (Persian numerals).

Do not serve duplicate copies from `public/fonts`; `next/font` emits assets under `/_next/static/media/`.

## Tailwind (v4)

Map tokens in `@theme inline`, e.g. `--font-sans: var(--font-peyda-fanum), …` and optional `--font-peyda`, `--font-rokh`, `--font-kaghaz` for `font-peyda` / `font-rokh` / `font-kaghaz` utilities.

## Storefront (v3 Tailwind)

[`apps/frontend/tailwind.config.ts`](apps/frontend/tailwind.config.ts) already references `var(--font-peyda-fanum)` etc.; keep that in sync with the variable names exported by `@repo/fonts`.
